CURRENT PROBLEM

In the BlueMind iOS side menu, when the user scrolls the menu content upward, rows/text can continue behind:

- BlueMind AI
- CHAT MODES
- the Search button

Because the header area is effectively transparent, the scrolling text remains fully sharp and visible underneath the header.

The result is visual overlap: text appears on top of/behind other text.

This is clearly visible on the real iPhone.

DESIRED IOS BEHAVIOR

I want behavior similar to modern native iOS / the attached reference:

The header remains visually floating.

As scrolling content approaches and passes underneath the header, it should:

1. remain visible normally lower on the screen;
2. gradually become blurred/faded as it enters the header boundary;
3. disappear cleanly before visually colliding with the fixed header title/buttons.

It should feel like the scrolling content is moving behind a translucent glass layer.

IMPORTANT — DO NOT USE A SOLID BLACK HEADER

